    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, that makes sense. i'll try to be polite but firm like you said. i'm just sitting here in my living room with three blankets on and it's still so cold. \n\nit just feels so weird though... like, there was nothing wrong yesterday. it was working fine, and then suddenly it's just dead. i keep looking at the radiator and wondering if there's like a tiny part that just snapped or something? do you think it could be something mechanical that just went wrong internally, or is it usually something more obvious like a pipe or a boiler issue?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
